# Concurrent agent coordination

- Inspect the branch and working-tree diff before editing.
- If another agent is active in the same branch, worktree, folder, or file
  scope, coordinate before touching overlapping files.
- Prefer direct agent messaging. Keep updates to at most four short lines:
  task, files or area, what and why, and the next conflicting action.
- `/kom <agent-or-task> <message>` invokes the project skill `kom`: contact the
  named existing agent now and report whether the message was delivered.
- Do not create a new agent merely to satisfy `/kom`. If live delivery is not
  available, use the secret-free coordination note below and say so explicitly.
- If direct messaging is unavailable, use a secret-free temporary note at
  `.agents/coordination/<agent-id>.md`. Remove or finish it when done.
- Pause overlapping edits and agree on ownership, ordering, or a compatible
  split. Ask Jakob when materially different options remain roughly 50/50.
- Never overwrite, discard, stage, commit, or rewrite another agent's changes
  without agreement. Recheck status and diff immediately before staging.
